WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.593
A digital footprint is the information created, collected, or exposed through online activity, accounts, connected devices, services, public records, and technical infrastructure.

00:00:10.593 --> 00:00:20.736
It includes obvious material such as a public profile and less visible traces such as service logs, metadata, and indexed records.

00:00:20.736 --> 00:00:28.174
An active footprint comes from deliberate sharing: posts, comments, uploads, resumes, websites, or public code.

00:00:28.174 --> 00:00:36.063
A passive footprint is collected or exposed as activity occurs, sometimes without a clear publishing decision.

00:00:36.063 --> 00:00:43.050
Examples include tracking records, technical logs, search indexes, and data held by third parties.

00:00:43.050 --> 00:00:47.332
Footprints can be personal, professional, organizational, or technical.

00:00:47.332 --> 00:00:51.164
A professional profile may reveal work history.

00:00:51.164 --> 00:00:56.348
An organization may expose domains, job postings, documents, and partners.

00:00:56.348 --> 00:01:02.885
Technical systems leave observable records such as certificates, public services, and software characteristics.

00:01:02.885 --> 00:01:08.970
These traces matter because they affect privacy, security, safety, reputation, and investigations.

00:01:08.970 --> 00:01:16.408
One detail may seem harmless, but several accurate details can combine into a sensitive picture.

00:01:16.408 --> 00:01:23.846
Old or incorrect information can also create risk when it is treated as current fact.

00:01:23.846 --> 00:01:32.186
Legitimate defensive analysis can identify unnecessary exposure, support incident response, verify organizational assets, and improve privacy controls.

00:01:32.186 --> 00:01:40.074
It should be bounded by purpose, authority, proportionality, and respect for people affected by the information.

00:01:40.074 --> 00:01:46.160
A digital footprint is not a complete identity or a guaranteed truth.

00:01:46.160 --> 00:01:53.147
It is a changing set of observable traces that must be interpreted in context.

00:01:53.147 --> 00:02:01.487
Responsible work validates sources, minimizes personal data, and uses findings to reduce risk rather than exploit individuals.
